        "text": "[?][?] 4 25",
        "@annotation": {
         "@id": "copies/my670qk6863#transcription-annotation",
         "belief": {
          "@type": "belief",
          "@id": "copies/my670qk6863#transcription-belief",
          "certainty": "likely",
          "reasons": [
           {
            "@type": "meaningComprehension",
            "comprehends": [
             "copies/my670qk6863#inscription"
            ],
            "note": "Graded medium on the figures of the date: one figure is arguable. Stamped, not written, running across the roll; five figures of which the last three (4, 2, 5) are plain. The first figure carries the foot serif and top flag of a 1 but is only half inked, and the second shows a bottom bowl alone, so the day is left unread. Any sane split of the five figures leaves month 4 and year 25, hence 1925-04. The roll number 2673 is in pencil in crop 2 and on the printed label in crop 4 (WELTE-MIGNON No. 2673, Hymns, played by E. Adam). Crop 3 perforations only."
           }
          ]
         }
        }
       }
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
